## Source of the GPL and LGPL packages

The mirrored images, and the images built on them (`agentry-codex`,
`agentry-hostlink`, `agentry-files`, `agentry-unsafe-kali` and
`agentry-browser`), carry Debian, Kali and Alpine packages, many under
the GNU GPL and LGPL. The packages in them are the distribution's own,
unchanged, and each distribution publishes the corresponding source of its
packages. For the exact version in an image, the package's version is in its
package database (`/var/lib/dpkg/status` on Debian and Kali,
`/lib/apk/db/installed` on Alpine) and its licence in
`/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright` (Debian, Kali).

- Debian (`agentry-python-slim`, `agentry-debian` and `agentry-browser`,
  trixie; `agentry-node-bookworm`, bookworm): https://sources.debian.org/ for
  browsing, https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/ for the source archives, and
  https://snapshot.debian.org/ for a version that is no longer in the
  archive. `agentry-browser`'s packages all come from the snapshot named in
  its record (`/etc/agentry/browser/record`), whose source archives are at
  `https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/<snapshot>/pool/` and
  `https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/<snapshot>/pool/`.
- Kali (`agentry-kali-rolling`, `agentry-unsafe-kali`): the source files in
  the package pool, http://http.kali.org/kali/pool/main/ (and `non-free` and
  `contrib` beside it).
- Alpine (the `agentry-*alpine*` images, `agentry-codex`, `agentry-hostlink`,
  `agentry-files`): the package recipes (`APKBUILD`) and patches in
  https://github.com/alpinelinux/aports at the branch named for the
  release in the image's `/etc/alpine-release`, for example `3.22-stable`;
  each recipe names the upstream source archive it builds.

